--- C6_before_C47_corollary
+++ C6_after_C47_corollary
@@ -1,3 +1,11 @@
-C.46 supplies a further exact limitation: $\Delta$ does not factor
-through the actual action on the full quotient $F/F'''$, since
-one full parity-one element induces literal identity there.
+C.46 supplies an exact lower bound: one full parity-one element has
+normalized conjugator in $F^{(3)}$ and induces literal identity on
+$F/F'''$. By its definition in C.14, the order-$442368$
+envelope is $F$ modulo the intersection of the kernels of all
+surjections $F\to S_4$; hence it embeds in the finite product of
+those $S_4$ targets. Each has trivial third derived subgroup.
+That same actual element therefore
+has the identity normalized residue in the order-$442368$ envelope,
+while its parity is one. C.47 proves the matching fourth-derived bound
+for retained normalized conjugators; it does not identify the kernel
+of the outer action at that derived level.
